Toga Fashion House Inventory Management System
A Django‑based application for managing clients, inventory records, deposits, and staff accountability at Toga Fashion House.
This system streamlines financial tracking, deposit history, and payment status updates, ensuring clarity and efficiency for both staff and management.

🚀 Features
Client Management: Register and manage client records.

Inventory Tracking: Record materials, charges, deposits, balances, and collection dates.

Deposit Management: Add multiple deposits per inventory item with automatic balance updates.

Payment Status: Auto‑update “Paid Fully” status and date when balance reaches zero.

Audit Logging: Track changes to inventory records for accountability.

User Roles: Separate dashboards for users and admins.

Responsive UI: Clean Bootstrap 5 interface with fixed navigation bar.

🛠️ Tech Stack
Backend: Django (Python)

Frontend: Bootstrap 5, FontAwesome

Database: SQLite (default) or PostgreSQL/MySQL (recommended for production)

Audit Logging: django‑auditlog

Authentication: Django’s built‑in user system

⚙️ Installation
Clone the repository

bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/toga-fashion-house.git
cd toga-fashion-house
Create and activate a virtual environment

bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Linux/Mac
venv\Scripts\activate      # Windows
Install dependencies

bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
Run migrations

bash
python manage.py migrate
Create a superuser

bash
python manage.py createsuperuser
Collect static files

bash
python manage.py collectstatic
Start the development server

bash
python manage.py runserver
📖 Usage
Log in via the dashboard.

Add clients and create inventory records.

Record deposits; balances update automatically.

View deposit history and payment status.

Use the admin dashboard for full control.

🔒 Deployment Checklist
Set DEBUG = False in settings.py.

Configure ALLOWED_HOSTS with your domain/IP.

Use a production database (PostgreSQL/MySQL).

Set up a proper web server (Gunicorn + Nginx recommended).

Configure static files with collectstatic.

Secure with HTTPS (SSL certificate).

